<title>LITHUANIA: BOURSE CAPITALISATION DOWN.</title>
<headline>BOURSE CAPITALISATION DOWN.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The capitalisation of the</p>
<p>Vilnius bourse fell to 5.211 billion litas last week from 5.255</p>
<p>billion litas the previous week, the stock exchange said on</p>
<p>Monday.</p>
<p>Vilnius bourse statistics:</p>
<p>					    June 16-20     June 09-13</p>
<p>    Submitted orders		  16,367	   14,436</p>
<p>    Executed orders		   1,079	    1,276</p>
<p>Number of transactions on</p>
<p>    Central market (CM)	     865		932</p>
<p>    Turnover on the CM in LTL     2,314,210	2,094,280</p>
<p>Number of transactions in</p>
<p>    block trades (BT)		 107		124</p>
<p>    Turnover of BT in LTL	   12,033,210     7,427,650</p>
<p>    Supply of shares per week     59,209,584     61,255,197</p>
<p>    Demand of shares per week     4,118,952	3,012,449</p>
<p>Turnover of shares</p>
<p>    on CM per week in LTL	   2,262,170	2,089,500</p>
<p>    in BT per week in LTL	   12,033,210     6,938,780</p>
<p>The number of transactions</p>
<p>    in government T-bills	   4		  3</p>
<p>The turnover of government</p>
<p>    T-bills in LTL per week	 52,035	   493,640</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom + 370 2 22 35 17</p>
</text>
